The battle of the bases is nicely outlined here:

http://www.packetgnomes.org/~chris/essays/base12.html

they say that we can only keep track of about 7 (+-2) things at a time, so
perhaps 8 is the better base, supported by the high regularity of it's early
decimals.

I certainly like 12 more than 10 for it's early prime divisibility, but if
you're going ideal, you may as well be bold and go for 60!

